(version 1)

# Board rules of ZoneFlow rev A. The fab limits are in hardware/rules/jlcpcb.kicad_dru.
# The reasons are in docs/design/hardware-layout.md.

# The keep-alive net (hardware design, section 8.5): no other track within 1 mm of its tracks.
# Pads are left out: at the module and at the 0603 resistors the neighbours are closer than that.
(rule "keep-alive guard"
  (condition "A.NetName == '/KA' && A.Type == 'Track' && B.Type == 'Track' && B.NetName != '/KA'")
  (constraint clearance (min 1.0mm)))

# The high-impedance nodes of the keep-alive detectors (net class HiZ, 0.6 mm): their own pads are
# as close to their neighbours as the parts make them. The wide clearance is for what is routed.
(rule "high-impedance nodes at their pads"
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'HiZ' && A.Type == 'Pad'")
  (constraint clearance (min 0.2mm)))

# The solder jumper JP1 bridges the contact of relay K1 on a board built without the relay. Its
# two pads, AC_L and COM, are 0.3 mm apart in KiCad's footprint, closer than the 0.5 mm of their
# class: that is what makes it bridgeable. The two nets are joined whenever the relay is closed.
# This is the one pair of pads on the board that is closer than its net class allows.
(rule "solder jumper JP1: pads 0.3 mm apart by design"
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad' && A.memberOfFootprint('JP1') && B.memberOfFootprint('JP1')")
  (constraint clearance (min 0.25mm)))
